    <node id="ba18b592-5c3b-46f9-b5cd-466f48ee9652">
      <data key="d0">{"name":"Life Insurance Policy Terms","text":" the 31-day period following the premium \n    due date during which coverage continues without lapse.\n\n4.4 \"Policy Anniversary\" means the same day and month as the \n    issue date in each subsequent year.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION 5: DEATH BENEFIT\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n5.1 We will pay the death benefit to the beneficiary if:\n    (a) The insured dies while this policy is in force, and\n    (b) We receive proof of death acceptable to us, and\n    (c) The death occurs before the policy expiry date.\n\n5.2 The death benefit will be paid in one lump sum unless the \n    beneficiary chooses an alternate settlement option.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION 6: PREMIUM PAYMENTS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n6.1 Premiums are due monthly on the 15th of each month.\n\n6.2 If a premium is not paid by the due date, a grace period of \n    31 days is allowed. Coverage continues during the grace period.\n\n6.3 If the premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, \n    the policy will lapse and coverage will terminate.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION 7: EXCLUSIONS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n7.1 SUICIDE CLAUSE: If the insured commits suicide within two \n    years from the issue date, our liability is limited to a \n    refund of premiums paid.\n\n7.2 No other exclusions apply to this policy.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION 8: CONVERSION PRIVILEGE\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n8.1 You may convert this policy to a permanent life insurance \n    policy without evidence of insurability.\n\n8.2 Conversion must occur before the earlier of:\n    (a) The policy expiry date, or\n    (b) The insured's 65th birthday.\n\n8.3 The premium for the new policy will be based on:\n    (a) The insured's attained age at conversion\n    (b) The amount of coverage converted\n    (c) The class of permanent policy selected\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nSECTION 9","summary":"This document details essential terms of a life insurance policy, including a 31-day grace period after the premium due date during which coverage remains effective. Death benefits are payable upon proof of death before the policy’s expiry, typically as a lump sum. Premiums are due monthly, and failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse. A suicide exclusion applies within the first two years, limiting payout to refunded premiums. Policyholders can convert to permanent insurance without medical evidence before age 65 or policy expiration, with premiums recalculated based on current age and chosen coverage.","topics":["Grace Period","Death Benefit","Premium Payments","Conversion Privilege"],"facts":[{"name":"Grace Period Definition","sentence":"The grace period is a 31-day period following the premium due date.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["grace period","premium payment","coverage continuation"],"entities":[{"name":"grace period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"period allowing late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days"]},{"name":"the 15th of each month","type":"DATE","role":"monthly premium due date","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy Anniversary","type":"POLICY_TERM","role":"annual renewal reference point","relational_anchors":["same day and month as the issue date"]},{"name":"death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"lump-sum payout upon qualifying death","relational_anchors":["paid in one lump sum"]},{"name":"suicide clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on insurer liability after suicide","relational_anchors":["within two years from the issue date"]},{"name":"conversion privilege","type":"CONCEPT","role":"right to switch to permanent policy","relational_anchors":["without evidence of insurability"]},{"name":"policy expiry date","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for policy continuation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"insured's 65th birthday","type":"DATE","role":"age limit for conversion eligibility","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Grace Period Continuation","sentence":"Coverage continues without lapse during the grace period.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["grace period","coverage continuity","premium payment delay"],"entities":[{"name":"grace period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"period allowing late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days"]},{"name":"the 15th of each month","type":"DATE","role":"monthly premium due date","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy Anniversary","type":"POLICY_TERM","role":"annual renewal reference point","relational_anchors":["same day and month as the issue date"]},{"name":"death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"lump-sum payout upon qualifying death","relational_anchors":["paid in one lump sum"]},{"name":"suicide clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on insurer liability after suicide","relational_anchors":["within two years from the issue date"]},{"name":"conversion privilege","type":"CONCEPT","role":"right to switch to permanent policy","relational_anchors":["without evidence of insurability"]},{"name":"policy expiry date","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for policy continuation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"insured's 65th birthday","type":"DATE","role":"age limit for conversion eligibility","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Grace Period Coverage","sentence":"The grace period allows continued coverage even if the premium is not paid by the due date.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["grace period","premium payment","coverage continuation"],"entities":[{"name":"grace period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"period allowing late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days"]},{"name":"the 15th of each month","type":"DATE","role":"monthly premium due date","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy Anniversary","type":"POLICY_TERM","role":"annual renewal reference point","relational_anchors":["same day and month as the issue date"]},{"name":"death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"lump-sum payout upon qualifying death","relational_anchors":["paid in one lump sum"]},{"name":"suicide clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on insurer liability after suicide","relational_anchors":["within two years from the issue date"]},{"name":"conversion privilege","type":"CONCEPT","role":"right to switch to permanent policy","relational_anchors":["without evidence of insurability"]},{"name":"policy expiry date","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for policy continuation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"insured's 65th birthday","type":"DATE","role":"age limit for conversion eligibility","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Policy Lapse After Grace Period","sentence":"If the premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy will lapse.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["grace period","premium non-payment","policy lapse"],"entities":[{"name":"grace period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"period allowing late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days"]},{"name":"the 15th of each month","type":"DATE","role":"monthly premium due date","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy Anniversary","type":"POLICY_TERM","role":"annual renewal reference point","relational_anchors":["same day and month as the issue date"]},{"name":"death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"lump-sum payout upon qualifying death","relational_anchors":["paid in one lump sum"]},{"name":"suicide clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on insurer liability after suicide","relational_anchors":["within two years from the issue date"]},{"name":"conversion privilege","type":"CONCEPT","role":"right to switch to permanent policy","relational_anchors":["without evidence of insurability"]},{"n