      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is a defining characteristic of the 20-Year Level Term Life Insurance policy, specifying its payout capacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="7f8cb083-f7ed-4837-a460-150e15a7c2d1">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $500,000 death benefit implies a specific financial obligation linked to the insured’s demise, reinforcing the significance of identifying the insured—John Michael Anderson—as central to the policy's purpose.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="68115e7f-f7b6-423f-93fb-d3d8750f2e29">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is payable specifically to the designated primary beneficiary, Sarah Elizabeth Anderson, should the insured pass away during the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">payee of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="24f6a5ad-25db-42dc-939d-c4d5b2ed9a0f">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is fully allocated to Sarah Elizabeth Anderson as the designated primary beneficiary, meaning she receives the entire sum upon the insured’s death.</data>
      <data key="d4">fully allotted to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="086e886c-9134-4e1e-85d7-0fcdb31e485b">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is intended for Sarah Elizabeth Anderson, whose status as the insured’s spouse explains her eligibility as the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">justifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
