      <data key="d3">The death benefit of $500,000 establishes the financial payout available under the policy, which would be distributed to contingent beneficiaries such as Emma Grace Anderson if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="7f9cc4e6-7309-41fc-89b5-a0f2bf367607">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit serves as the basis for calculating Lucas’s share, which is determined to be 50% based on equal distribution among contingent beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
