    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">The 'Premium Due Date' being the 15th of each month sets the deadline from which the 31-day grace period begins, ensuring continuous coverage if paid within that window.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the monthly deadline for premium payment, which initiates the subsequent 31-day grace period mentioned in fact_sentence_2, allowing uninterrupted coverage despite late payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the monthly premium due date as the 15th, establishing the critical deadline; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that missing this deadline—and any subsequent payments within the 31-day grace period—results in policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the monthly due date for premiums, which triggers the start of the grace period mentioned in fact_sentence_2; thus, adherence to the due date prevents policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the precise due date (the 15th) for premiums, providing concrete support for the more general claim in fact_sentence_2 that payments are due monthly on the 15th.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes the specific due date (the 15th) for premiums, which contextualizes when the 31-day grace period begins—making it clear that coverage continues until the 15th plus 31 days. This supports understanding of timely payments and consequences of delay.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 defines the monthly deadline for premium payment, which initiates the 31-day grace period described in fact sentence 2, ensuring continuity of coverage despite late payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The specified premium due date ensures timely payments necessary to maintain policy validity, thereby supporting the condition under which the death benefit is payable.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The specified premium due date ensures continuous coverage until the policy expires, enabling the death benefit to be paid if the insured dies before termination. Without timely payments, coverage lapses, nullifying the benefit even if death occurs early.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th of each month ensures timely payments that maintain active coverage, enabling the death benefit to be paid out per the conditions outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th of each month enables consistent policy status, ensuring continued eligibility for conversion into permanent insurance without evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th ensures ongoing coverage necessary for meeting the condition of converting to permanent insurance before age 65 or policy end.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th of each month sets the timing for ongoing payments, while the concept of converting to permanent insurance depends on the insured’s age at that time, potentially affecting future premium amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th of each month sets the timeline for payments required under the original policy, which directly informs when the premium adjustments for a future conversion would take effect.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The defined premium due date (15th of the month) establishes a recurring obligation under the current term policy, while the second fact indicates that any future permanent policy would have premiums determined by its classification—a condition that could alter the original due date's significance if conversion happens.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th of each month sets the deadline for payments, but the grace period ensures uninterrupted coverage even if payment occurs later, making timely payment more flexible.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The fixed premium due date on the 15th ensures ongoing coverage, enabling the insurer to process claims only if the policyholder has maintained compliance; thus, adherence to this deadline supports the condition required for proving death and receiving benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
