    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">The grace period is explicitly stated as lasting 31 days after the premium due date, providing time for payment without losing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">defines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that coverage continues past the due date, allowing time for late payments while maintaining eligibility for benefits. However, even with ongoing coverage, the insurer requires official proof of death to disburse the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows additional time to pay the overdue premium without losing coverage. If payment isn't made by its conclusion, the policy terminates.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continuous coverage beyond the due date, potentially enabling the death benefit to be claimed even if the premium was late, so long as death occurs before policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows continued coverage even if the premium is not paid by the due date. This ensures uninterrupted protection during the specified window.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period begins immediately after the monthly premium due date, ensuring continuous coverage if paid within that window.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary leeway after the premium due date, allowing continued coverage despite late payment. If the premium isn't settled by its conclusion, coverage ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that coverage remains active even if the premium payment is delayed beyond the due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 defines the grace period as lasting 31 days after the premium due date. This definition directly supports fact sentence 2, which confirms that such a 31-day grace period is permitted when a premium is unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">rephrases</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
