      <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the 31-day grace period triggers policy lapse. This outcome hinges on the predefined length of the grace period established earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium by the end of the grace period triggers policy lapse, meaning the protection from fact_sentence_1 ceases.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period triggers policy lapse, underscoring the importance of the grace period's role in maintaining active coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that non-payment beyond the grace period causes the policy to lapse, which directly implies termination of coverage, aligning precisely with fact sentence 2's assertion.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, meaning no future benefits—including death benefits—are available. Therefore, even if proof of death is submitted later, it cannot trigger a payout unless the policy was still active at the time of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it is no longer active. As a result, the death benefit cannot be paid because the policy is not in force at the time of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums are due monthly on the 15th sets the timeline against which the 31-day grace period operates, helping determine if a late payment falls outside the grace window.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual dependency</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The policy's continuation during the grace period ensures that beneficiaries remain protected until payment is made, creating a buffer before any lapse occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payments without immediate consequences, creating a buffer that prevents automatic lapses when premiums are late.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to missed payment beyond the grace period, the opportunity to convert to permanent insurance expires because the policy is no longer active.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, meaning that if death occurs after the lapse but before expiry, the death benefit cannot be claimed since the policy is no longer active.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, preventing any further actions like conversion. The premium calculation at conversion depends on the insured's age at that time, but this option is unavailable once the policy lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Without payment by the end of the 31-day grace period, the policy terminates—highlighting why the grace period's existence is conditional on prompt renewal.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
