    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="29888d17-fc84-4f64-919e-e477c85d7da6">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force—including during the grace period—the death benefit becomes payable. Therefore, the existence of an active policy status, maintained through the grace period, supports the condition required for benefit disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force—including during the grace period—the death benefit is payable, making the grace period critical for maintaining eligibility under fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit hinges on the policy being in force at the time of death. Since the grace period preserves the policy's status during delays in premium payments, it enables the fulfillment of this financial commitment by preventing premature lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy is still in effect at the time of death. This requires that the premium has been paid within the grace period; otherwise, the policy would have lapsed, making the benefit non-payable.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the insured dies while the policy is in effect. This means that any lapse caused by missing payments beyond the grace period would prevent the payout, making timely premium payment critical.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable upon the insured's death while the policy is in force, but only if that death happens prior to the policy's expiry date. Without meeting this time constraint, even an otherwise eligible claim would not result in a payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only triggered if the policyholder's death occurs while the policy is active, but it cannot be paid out unless official proof of death is submitted by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">requires proof</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force, the death benefit becomes payable. This benefit is typically issued as a lump sum unless otherwise selected by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">payment method</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable only if the insured dies while the policy is in force, which includes the grace period when premiums are overdue but coverage persists.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 does not apply if the insured dies by suicide within two years of the policy's issue date, as specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the core condition for death benefit payment. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that only known exclusions (like suicide) exist, reinforcing confidence in the claim eligibility defined by sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures the policy stays active beyond the due date, preserving eligibility for the death benefit if the insured passes away during this time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy remains in force, which depends on consistent premium payments made according to the specified schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit depends on the policy being active at the time of death, which may require actions like conversion by age 65 to maintain that status. Conversion availability ensures ongoing coverage options that support sustained eligibility for benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 may depend on whether the policyholder converts coverage, as the resulting policy's terms—and thus its payout potential—are influenced by the amount of coverage selected at conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
