      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 depends on the existence of an active policy; the grace period described in fact_sentence_1 preserves policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit when the insured passes away.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the trigger for paying the death benefit; fact_sentence_1 clarifies what the death benefit actually is, providing necessary meaning to the event described in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit hinges on the policy being active, which depends on premiums being paid by the due date—specifically the 15th of the month—as defined here.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
