    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">To receive the death benefit, proof of death must be submitted. This requirement stands independently of whether the policyholder used the 31-day grace period to maintain coverage through a missed payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Even though coverage may continue past the due date via the grace period, the death benefit cannot be issued without proper proof of death being verified.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Receiving proof of death is required to initiate the death benefit process, which assumes the policy remained in force—such as through timely payment or use of the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">To receive the death benefit, proof of death must be provided. However, if the policy has already lapsed due to missed payments beyond the grace period, such proof becomes irrelevant because the policyholder would no longer have an active policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary to receive the death benefit; however, such a claim cannot succeed if coverage was already terminated due to missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">Receipt of proof of death is mandatory for processing the death benefit; without such documentation, even an active policy does not result in a payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 requires proof of death to initiate benefit payment; however, such proof is only relevant if the death occurred before the policy expired, making it contingent on the timing specified in fact sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted to initiate the claims process; only after verification is the death benefit distributed, typically as a lump sum unless otherwise selected by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of death depends on continued coverage; if coverage lapses, no claim can be made. The grace period ensures continuity, enabling the process outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for proof of death is subject to a restriction if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, in which case the insurer's obligation is reduced to returning premiums rather than paying the full death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The need for proof of death to trigger the death benefit is confirmed as the sole procedural requirement, since no other policy exclusions limit eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for claiming benefits, regardless of the permanent policy class selected during conversion; however, the choice of policy class impacts whether conversion is viable at all.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to claim the death benefit; the grace period allows the policyholder's estate sufficient time post-due date to provide such documentation without losing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death, mentioned in fact_sentence_2, is necessary to trigger the death benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1, making it an essential prerequisite for claim settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for claiming the death benefit, but such a claim can only succeed if the policy was not lapsed—meaning premiums were paid on time, particularly by the 15th of each month as specified.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
