    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid, the insured must die before the policy expires, meaning timely premium payments—including those made during the grace period—are necessary to maintain coverage until that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">temporal condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the insured must die before policy expiry; this requirement relies on continued coverage, maintained through the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to apply, the death must occur prior to policy expiry; thus, the existence of a grace period increases the window during which such deaths could qualify, reinforcing its importance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the policy must remain in effect until death; therefore, timely premium payment—even within the grace period—is necessary to maintain eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for payment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the policy must still be active; thus, timely premium payments ensuring continued coverage are required prior to death.</data>
      <data key="d4">precondition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">Death benefits are contingent on the insured dying prior to policy expiry, meaning the policy’s end date—a fixed point determined at inception—is critical. The 'Policy Anniversary' serves as an annual reference point used to monitor how close the policy is to expiring.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid under the policy, the insured must die before the policy ends; however, this depends on the policy being actively in force at the time of death, ensuring continuous coverage up to that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid under any circumstances, the insured must die before the policy expires; even with proper proof of death, payment is denied if the death occurs post-expiry, rendering the requirement in fact sentence 1 irrelevant otherwise.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage even after missing a premium, allowing the death benefit to remain applicable if death occurs during this extended timeframe prior to policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies before policy expiry, the death benefit generally applies; however, if the death is by suicide within two years, the benefit is restricted to a refund of premiums instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies when the death benefit is payable, while fact_sentence_2 confirms that no additional restrictions exist beyond what's already outlined, supporting the validity of the condition set forth in sentence one.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry ensures claim validity, while the 31-day grace period helps maintain active coverage despite missed payments, thereby preserving eligibility for the death benefit under the stated conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that the death benefit depends on the insured dying before the policy expires. This condition aligns with the timeframe mentioned in fact_sentence_2, which limits when conversion to permanent insurance may occur, emphasizing the importance of the policy expiry date as a critical boundary.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The conditionality of the death benefit depends on timely policy maintenance; however, the ability to convert to permanent insurance—affected by attained age—provides a pathway that could extend coverage beyond initial term limits, thereby potentially enabling future claim eligibility depending on when conversion occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry may be affected by the permanent policy class chosen during conversion, as different classes have varying terms and durations influencing when benefits become available.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry makes the grace period relevant, as it helps maintain active status long enough for claims to qualify when death happens near the deadline.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the temporal condition for payout; fact_sentence_1 explains the financial consequence of meeting that condition—the disbursement of the specified benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry depends on sustained premium payments; missing the 15th due date could trigger lapse unless covered by the grace period, thus linking the due date to benefit eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
