      <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid as a lump sum if the beneficiary opts for that settlement; however, this distribution requires prior submission and acceptance of proof of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is generally paid as a lump sum, but if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, the insurer's obligation is restricted to returning only the premiums paid, effectively nullifying the full lump-sum payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
