    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The choice of conversion amount affects long-term benefit outcomes, indirectly influencing whether beneficiaries receive payments via lump sum or alternative options later. However, it does not alter the immediate lump-sum default rule stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The default lump-sum payment of death benefits depends on the beneficiary's choices, but the available settlement options may vary depending on the permanent policy class selected during conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on the policy remaining active; the 31-day grace period preserves this activity, ensuring payouts remain possible despite delayed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on coverage</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the typical payment form of the death benefit—a lump sum—which directly supports and contextualizes the nature of the $500,000 benefit described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
