    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premiums due on the 15th trigger the start of the subsequent 31-day grace period if not paid by that date.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premiums due on the 15th establish the deadline that triggers the start of the 31-day grace period, ensuring continuous coverage until payment is made or the grace period expires.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premiums due on the 15th establish a recurring deadline that triggers the start of the 31-day grace period if unpaid, maintaining continuous protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium by the end of the grace period leads to policy lapse, meaning timely payment—on or before the 15th plus 31 days—is critical to maintaining coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">timing precondition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Knowing that premiums are due on the 15th allows one to determine whether the grace period has been exceeded if payment is delayed beyond that date plus 31 days.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premium payments ensure that the policy stays active, thereby allowing the death benefit to be paid out upon the insured's passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The monthly due date set on the 15th defines when the grace period begins if payment is not made, ensuring clarity about when coverage may still apply despite late payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums are due monthly on the 15th sets the trigger point for initiating the 31-day grace period if payment is delayed beyond that date.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums are due monthly provides the basis for determining whether any premiums were paid, which directly affects the amount recoverable under the suicide exclusion clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premium deadlines establish an ongoing obligation that could precede a future decision to convert. When conversion occurs, the new premium rate depends on the insured’s current age, reflecting updated risk assessment tied to long-term policy maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">Monthly premium deadlines ensure ongoing policy validity, allowing the holder to remain eligible for conversion by maintaining active status until age 65 or policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for monthly premium payments on the 15th creates the timing framework necessary for the 31-day grace period referenced in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Timely monthly premium payments on the 15th ensure continued policy coverage, enabling the death benefit specified in fact_sentence_1 to be paid upon the insured’s death during the term.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
