    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="73c9df30-adf1-47fa-a916-f047355da103">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that coverage does not lapse immediately upon missed payment, enabling continuous protection as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that a 31-day grace period is granted if a premium isn't paid on time. This aligns precisely with fact sentence 1's assertion that the grace period lasts 31 days post-due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">rephrases</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the length of the grace period as 31 days; fact_sentence_1 confirms that such a period ensures ongoing coverage when payments are delayed beyond the due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Without the grace period, the condition specified in fact_sentence_1—policy lapse due to missed payments—would occur immediately, eliminating any delay in enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Without the 31-day grace period, the consequence of non-payment—coverage termination—would occur immediately, but the grace period explicitly defers that outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period enables ongoing coverage, thereby maintaining the conditions necessary for the death benefit to be paid.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period preserves policy effectiveness past the due date, ensuring continued coverage so that a death occurring before policy expiry may still qualify for the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables eligibility</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid by the 15th—the established due date—then the policyholder enters a 31-day grace period allowing continued coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows late payment of premiums, maintaining coverage temporarily; this continuity enables potential future options such as converting to permanent insurance, where updated premiums depend on the individual's current age.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate loss of coverage, giving policyholders additional flexibility that could impact decisions about converting the policy later. This window does not alter the deadline for conversion, which is fixed at age 65 or policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">temporal dependency</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time for payment after the due date, ensuring that coverage does not terminate immediately upon missed payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage after missing a premium payment, providing breathing room that supports ongoing eligibility for future actions like converting the policy. This temporal stability indirectly enables the possibility of conversion later.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states a general rule about grace periods, which is exemplified and contextualized by fact_sentence_1 through its application in a specific life insurance policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on continued coverage; the 31-day grace period allows uninterrupted eligibility for the benefit despite missed premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies a 31-day grace period after the due date, which aligns with and validates the automatic deduction schedule mentioned in fact sentence 1, confirming that late payments do not immediately terminate coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage beyond the due date, allowing time to consider conversion into a permanent policy, where the choice of class impacts the final terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to maintain active status, enabling timely conversion decisions; however, the final conversion result depends on the specific amount of coverage elected, influencing long-term policy viability post-grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
