    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage during an unpaid premium period requires a predefined grace period; here, it is explicitly set at 31 days.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that coverage endures despite an unpaid premium during the grace period. Fact_sentence_1 confirms this continuity broadly, aligning with the specific scenario described in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period triggers policy lapse, meaning the protection offered during the grace period ceases if no action is taken.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 affirms ongoing coverage during the grace period despite non-payment. This directly supports fact sentence 1's claim about the grace period enabling uninterrupted protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Because coverage remains effective throughout the grace period even if the premium is unpaid, the eventual lapse described in fact_sentence_1 depends directly on missing the deadline set by this grace window.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage during the grace period allows the policyholder's death to still qualify for the death benefit, ensuring eligibility even if the premium was not yet paid.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage during the grace period allows sufficient time for beneficiaries to provide proof of death, making it possible to fulfill the condition required for death benefit disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage during the grace period supports the validity of the death benefit claim, ensuring it can be paid if death happens before policy expiry, despite late premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid by the 15th, the policyholder retains coverage for an additional 31 days, meaning the grace period depends directly on the fixed due date specified earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage during the grace period depends entirely on the existence of the 31-day window granted after the premium's due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage even if a premium is delayed, and the absence of further exclusions confirms that this provision operates without limitation from other restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that coverage continues during the grace period, which is further clarified and contextualized by fact_sentence_1 specifying its length and timing relative to the premium due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on continued coverage; therefore, its availability hinges on policies like the grace period maintaining validity until renewal or lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary coverage continuity, allowing the insured sufficient time to decide on converting the policy; since conversion outcomes depend on attained age, maintaining coverage during the grace period ensures eligibility for timely conversion at favorable rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period depends on having a defined premium due date—established here as the 15th—to determine when the grace period starts, linking it back to the scheduled payment timeline.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">Coverage during the grace period ensures uninterrupted protection until renewal, which may influence timing and decision-making related to converting coverage; however, the actual conversion result depends on the selected coverage amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage despite late payments, enabling time to consider converting to a permanent policy, where the specific class selected determines the final terms and benefits received.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
