    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The absence of additional exclusions ensures broader validity of the death benefit provision outlined in fact_sentence_1, making it more likely that claims will succeed unless specifically barred.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The statement that no other exclusions apply ensures that the requirement for submitting proof of death stands as the primary and final condition for claiming the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 asserts the absence of further exclusions, thereby validating that the requirement in fact_sentence_1—that death occur before policy expiry—is the sole temporal limitation affecting claim eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The lack of additional exclusions means that the grace period rule stands unchallenged, allowing uninterrupted coverage during the specified window after missed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">There are no further exclusions beyond the suicide clause in the first two years, meaning the limitation described in the prior sentence fully defines the policy's exclusion framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The statement about no other exclusions implies that standard policy conditions govern conversions, allowing the insurer to base new premiums solely on the insured's attained age at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The statement about no other exclusions reinforces the scope of the policy's provisions, ensuring that the conversion right described in the second sentence is fully applicable without hidden restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="284998d7-5a28-4d62-b70a-2a1cd03760d8" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
