    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical evidence depends on completing the conversion before either the policy expires or the insured turns 65.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance allows policyholders to switch policies without proving insurability, and the resulting premium depends on the specific class of permanent policy they choose.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">Converting to permanent insurance allows the policyholder to secure coverage without medical exams; the resulting premium is calculated using the individual's actual age at the time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance allows policyholders to switch plans without proving health status; the premium for the new plan is calculated according to the specific amount of coverage they select.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The availability of converting to permanent insurance without medical evidence implies an important exception to typical underwriting rules, which aligns with the claim that no further exclusions exist beyond what is specified.</data>
      <data key="d4">implied by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance offers long-term protection options regardless of health changes, making it relevant even when considering missed payments and grace periods, though it doesn't rely on them.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance relies on maintaining active status—supported by the 31-day grace period—which prevents immediate lapse and preserves eligibility for conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">The option to convert the policy enables sustained eligibility for the death benefit beyond the fixed term, making the conversion right functionally dependent on maintaining the underlying death benefit provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">Conversion rights depend on sustained policy validity; thus, meeting the monthly premium deadline on the 15th preserves the ability to exercise this option later.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6257cee7-cf80-47c1-ad60-b54fa71a0daa" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">expires at</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="70980adf-3ba4-4e14-bcaa-8fe1839c7e8d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="c60749d9-dc8a-427a-bf3d-ad9a6776fa1f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="872bbbda-6914-4ad7-b1e5-a6d4812dbcc7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">policy term</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="faa18015-884a-4a4e-ae61-8121c4bf976b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="3a7b483b-8402-4733-9479-489257de9c66">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="cd6932e7-27c9-4093-bbb5-5e2872c73afe">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="e3edf6ca-a1f8-47b9-9c0b-0fc991c06640">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="2552b992-ff83-4048-a191-15ee02954a95">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry sets a critical deadline for policy changes. This constraint means that while the grace period offers flexibility post-due-date, it doesn’t extend the window for conversion decisions beyond the specified cutoff dates.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on time</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Conversion rights expire at age 65 or policy end date, so acting within those limits becomes critical. Since the grace period delays lapses, it indirectly supports decision-making around conversion before such cutoffs.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry ensures that holders retain an option to switch policies only while still eligible, but this benefit is nullified if the policy lapses from unpaid premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry depends on maintaining active coverage, which requires paying premiums within the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on coverage</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry supports maintaining an active policy, thereby preserving the conditions necessary for the death benefit to be payable when the insured passes away.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines a time limit for converting to permanent insurance, dependent on either reaching age 65 or policy expiry. Since the death benefit is only available before policy expiry, the same cutoff date governs both conversion eligibility and claim validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry necessitates timely premium payments to avoid lapses that would disqualify future conversion attempts.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry sets an upper limit on when conversion can happen; however, it does not affect the availability of the 31-day grace period for premium payments, which operates separately from conversion timelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">time constraint</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">To exercise the option of converting without evidence of insurability, the policyholder must act prior to reaching age 65 or the policy’s expiry date.</data>
      <data key="d4">required before</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The deadline for conversion affects when the insured reaches a certain age, which determines the premium rate under the new policy. Without meeting the conversion deadline, the opportunity to lock in a favorable rate based on current age is lost.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 or policy expiry enables the application of updated premiums based on the selected permanent policy type.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to convert before age 65 depends on sustained coverage; the grace period prevents lapses that could disqualify the insured from exercising this option.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a condition related to policy conversion prior to age 65 or policy end, which indirectly affects whether the death benefit may remain available beyond the initial term through a converted policy, though it doesn't define or modify the benefit's nature.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">Meeting the deadline for the premium due date is required to remain eligible for conversion to permanent insurance prior to age 65 or policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
