    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">When converting to permanent insurance, the premium is set according to the insured's attained age; this process may occur after using the grace period to maintain coverage post-due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for converted policies are set according to the insured's attained age, meaning timely action before lapse is necessary to access this benefit. Otherwise, the opportunity is lost entirely.</data>
      <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for converted policies are calculated using the insured’s attained age at conversion, meaning older ages lead to higher costs. This calculation assumes the policyholder has maintained coverage up to that point, possibly relying on grace periods to avoid lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to base premiums on the insured's attained age at conversion implies that the timing of conversion—such as on a policy anniversary—determines the applicable age factor in pricing.</data>
      <data key="d4">determined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance allows renewal without medical exams but only if done while the original policy is still active, meaning timely premium payments are required to maintain eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables reconversion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The determination of converted policy premiums using attained age implies that regular premium payments—such as those due monthly—are part of the continuous policy lifecycle leading up to potential conversion, though the exact due date has no bearing on the pricing mechanism itself.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for converted policies are determined by the insured’s attained age at time of conversion, meaning accurate tracking of enrollment timelines—including those affected by the 31-day grace period—is necessary to ensure proper calculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">Since the converted policy’s premium relies on the insured’s attained age, this necessitates that conversion occurs without requiring medical evidence, ensuring fairness and accessibility regardless of health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The rule that premiums depend on attained age at conversion aligns with typical policy practices, reinforcing that no unusual restrictions or exceptions override this standard mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The premium amount for the converted policy hinges on the insured's age at conversion, making it critical that conversion happens by the cutoff date tied to either the policy expiry or the 65th birthday.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The premium depends on the insured's age at conversion, but it also varies depending on the specific class of permanent policy chosen, meaning both elements contribute independently to the rate determination.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The premium depends on the insured's age when converting, and this age-based rate interacts with the level of coverage being converted, influencing the final premium amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance relies on the insured being alive and covered; the 31-day grace period preserves eligibility for such action by preventing immediate lapse after missing a premium, thereby supporting the practical application of age-based premium calculation at conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on grace period</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 discusses premium adjustments upon conversion based on age, it indirectly supports the ongoing validity of the death benefit defined in fact_sentence_1 by ensuring continued access to coverage through conversion, preserving the original benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
