    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The premium amount for the converted permanent policy is calculated according to its classification, which relies on the prior allowance of conversion without medical underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The determination of the new premium based on the policy class assumes that conversion has occurred within the allowed timeframe specified in the prior clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The choice of permanent policy class sets the baseline premium tier, which is further adjusted according to the insured's attained age at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The choice of permanent policy class directly affects the premium rate, which is adjusted according to the amount of coverage being converted into the new policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
