    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age influences how favorable the conversion terms may be, while the selected coverage amount determines the extent of protection post-conversion. Together, they shape the overall feasibility and cost of the new policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">An individual’s attained age influences the available options and premiums during conversion, which may limit or expand access to certain permanent policy classes. Conversely, selecting a specific policy class sets expectations for coverage and pricing that depend on the insured’s current age.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age determines eligibility and terms during conversion; if this age was incorrectly reported, the insurer adjusts the death benefit accordingly to match what could have been obtained at the true age.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry determines payout eligibility, but the option to convert to permanent insurance based on attained age offers a mechanism to maintain coverage past the original term, thus preserving potential access to death benefits through extended protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 focuses on how age at conversion shapes policy conversion outcomes, it does not alter the standard lump-sum payment rule for death benefits outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The impact of attained age on conversion determines whether the insured receives optimal terms; thus, preserving coverage during the grace period becomes crucial to avoid losing access to conversion options based on future aging effects.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
