    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The amount of coverage being converted depends on the insured’s current age, as older ages may limit available options or increase premiums. Thus, attainment age constrains the practicality of higher coverage amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The amount of coverage being converted influences how much protection is available under the new permanent policy, but its impact depends on the specific class of permanent policy selected, which defines the policy’s characteristics and cost structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The timing and conditions for paying the death benefit, outlined in fact_sentence_1, are affected by prior actions like converting coverage; the extent of conversion determines the final benefit level available upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_1 specifies that death benefits are generally paid as a lump sum, fact_sentence_2 explains that the size of converted coverage determines post-conversion benefit levels; thus, larger conversions may lead to higher eventual payouts, potentially affecting settlement preferences.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The extent of coverage chosen during conversion determines the final policy terms, though such conversions occur only under conditions where coverage—such as during a grace period—is still technically active.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The magnitude of converted coverage directly impacts the resulting policy terms, such as premiums and benefits, which could affect whether the policy remains viable through the 31-day grace period if renewal costs exceed available funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00e3af95-29f5-4b5e-8389-54426f3e7784" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines conversion outcome based on coverage amount</data>
    </edge>
