    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">Choosing a particular permanent policy class establishes baseline features like coverage level and cost, but its applicability depends on the insured’s attained age, which governs underwriting approval and rate classification.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The class of permanent policy selected sets the framework—such as premiums and benefits—for the converted coverage; therefore, it determines how effectively different amounts of coverage can be accommodated.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The timing and validity of the death benefit payment in fact_sentence_1 rely on maintaining active coverage, which can only occur through proper conversion to a permanent policy, making the selection of the policy class directly relevant to claim eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">While the class of permanent policy determines conversion success, it does not alter the fundamental need for documented proof of death to receive any resulting death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The condition for receiving a death benefit—payment only if death occurs before expiry—is influenced by the permanent policy class selected at conversion, since such choices determine ongoing coverage validity and benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">The outcome of converting to a permanent policy is influenced by the specific policy class chosen, which may determine whether alternative settlement methods beyond a lump sum are permitted.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">Choosing a particular permanent policy class impacts the conversion process, potentially influencing whether it's feasible or advantageous to convert during the grace period when coverage is still active.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Choosing a permanent policy class determines conversion outcomes, but only if done before the end of the grace period when premiums remain overdue.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
