      <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot dispute the policy terms, including those involving misstatements. This creates the condition under which the misstatement provision applies, allowing for benefit recalculations based on accurate information.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
