    <edge source="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains that if the insured's age was misrepresented, the death benefit is adjusted to match what could have been bought at the correct age. This logically connects to fact sentence 2, which applies the same principle to incorrect gender reporting, ensuring equitable adjustments regardless of the type of misstatement.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">When the insured’s age is misstated, the company recalculates the death benefit using the correct age; however, the specific adjusted amount depends on the insured’s sex at the time of the error.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997" target="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19">
      <data key="d3">The correction of the death benefit due to age misstatement hinges on identifying the insured’s true age at the time the error occurred, ensuring accurate recalibration of benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
