      <data key="d3">Adjustments to the death benefit due to misstated sex depend on accurate verification of the insured's identity and cause of death, necessitating official documents like a certified death certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">When a misstatement regarding the insured’s sex is identified after a claim is submitted, the insurer revises the death benefit accordingly—a step contingent upon initial claim filing as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc" target="48cefe40-498d-4ea8-8c59-1a68bc65d395">
      <data key="d3">Adjustments to the death benefit due to misstated sex rely on the existence of the incontestability period; without it, the insurer could challenge the policy entirely, nullifying any basis for recalculating benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that misreported sex leads to a recalculated death benefit reflecting the correct sex’s actuarial cost. This mirrors fact sentence 1, where misstated age triggers a similar correction, showing consistent application across demographic inaccuracies.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc" target="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19">
      <data key="d3">When the insured’s sex is misstated, the death benefit is adjusted according to the premiums paid; however, the exact corrected amount hinges on the insured’s age at the time of the error.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
