    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at misstatement directly influences the calculation of the revised death benefit, making it foundational to the adjustment process described in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at the time of misstatement directly influences the revised death benefit, especially when the misstated sex affects premium calculations and final payout amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit depends on the insured's age when the misstatement occurred; similarly, it also depends on the insured's sex at that time. Both attributes independently shape how the benefit is adjusted.</data>
      <data key="d4">equally relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
