    <edge source="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97" target="471c34c1-d1a8-4f71-8826-3551efd6d8aa">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy creates a scenario where the insurer explicitly avoids liability regarding the assignment's validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97" target="89eb9f0b-fb9d-4ed0-96df-faae58d5ebda">
      <data key="d3">The right to assign the policy relies on proper authorization, which is confirmed by the designated official's signature on relevant documents.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy depends on SecureLife Insurance Company's acknowledgment through written notice. Without this step, the assignment remains ineffective despite being initiated.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
