    <edge source="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">SecureLife does not recognize policy assignments without written notice at its home office, reinforcing the need for documented communication. Similarly, claims must also be submitted directly to SecureLife, underscoring consistent procedural expectations for interaction with the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The necessity for written notice arises because SecureLife disclaims responsibility for assignment validity, meaning it cannot act on an assignment without direct confirmation from the assignor.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9" target="89eb9f0b-fb9d-4ed0-96df-faae58d5ebda">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice to SecureLife Insurance Company regarding policy assignments relies on proper authentication, which may involve authorized signatures such as those from senior officers like the Chief Underwriting Officer.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9" target="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97">
      <data key="d3">SecureLife’s acceptance of written notice is required before any policy assignment becomes binding, meaning the initial assignment action cannot have legal force without it.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f234b0fb-111d-42e8-819d-5b778959f4be" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines binding status of assignment upon receipt of written notice</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c1b7ff5f-97ac-4bae-802d-f8443ca9a5dd" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">processes the notice leading to binding status</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4a21778e-3155-4d8a-a2b7-c58153adce41" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the required mailing address for notice</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="85f1b8db-cc6d-4fc5-b89c-1ee14fdb0d1b" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
